# A knob that dims an LED. Click RV1 and turn it.
#
# The potentiometer's track runs across the 9 V battery, its first end on ground and its other on
# the 9 V, so its wiper is anywhere from 0 V to 9 V as it is turned: halfway, 4.5 V. The wiper feeds
# the LED through R1, which keeps the current safe with the knob all the way up.
#
# Turned down, the wiper is below the 1.8 V the LED needs before it lights, and it stays dark. Turned
# up, the current rises with every step past that: about 1 mA halfway, and about 20 mA at the top,
# where only R1 holds it back.
#
# The meter reads the wiper.

battery  B1   0 0  0 8  9V
wire          0 0  6 0
pot      RV1  6 8  8 4  6 0  10k 50%
wire          0 8  6 8
ground        0 8

resistor R1   8 4  16 4  330
led      D1   16 4  16 8  red
wire          16 8  6 8

meter    WIPER  8 4  8 8
